# Counterfactual: the attester-independence conjunct stripped from the compensation rule
#
# Derivation is monotone and probe facts load on top, so no probe against the
# real constitution can show what `~($a = $payer)` prevents. This copy is the
# only way that claim is executed rather than argued: one conjunct removed, and
# the payer attesting its own promise starts counting.
:expect-pins 3
# The payer attests its own wage. Against the real constitution this derives
# nothing; here it derives the compensation.
promise(Firm, Wage, Ugo).
authorized(Firm, CompensationAttester, Ugo).
observe(Firm, Wage, Ugo, LabourBasis).
? provide(Firm, Wage, Ugo).
# => TRUE
# The independent route still works, so this fixture removes a guard rather
# than the rule.
promise(Firm, Wage, Tam).
authorized(Arbiter, CompensationAttester, Tam).
observe(Arbiter, Wage, Tam, LabourBasis).
? provide(Firm, Wage, Tam).
# => TRUE
# Only the compensation rule lost its guard: the restitution rule still refuses
# a payer-attested basis, which attributes the flip above to the one conjunct.
observe(Court, CompensationFraud, Ugo, LabourBasis).
? provide(Ugo, Restitution, Firm).
# => FALSE
